WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.552
You finished the class. Now see what changed.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.406
End the ride, and Wattzup saves it and opens its summary.

00:00:11.606 --> 00:00:14.890
Average power leads, with the change since last time.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.524
Every cadence dip is marked on the trace.

00:00:22.724 --> 00:00:25.596
Point at a dip in the list, and its band lights up.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.466
Beside it, your streak, this week's rides, and any best you set.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.056
Progress compares a class you have ridden more than once.

00:00:45.256 --> 00:00:49.521
Average power, cadence on target, or dips, attempt by attempt.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.341
Every saved ride is listed, with six weeks of streak and your achievements.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.619
On a phone, the summary and progress stack into one column.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.790
What the tests prove: a bike ride of a minute or more is saved, and kept after a

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:19.569
restart.

00:01:19.769 --> 00:01:23.292
Streaks and bests come from your own rides, never invented.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.864
That is journey fourteen. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:32.864 --> 00:01:34.197
training display.
